The '''school''' in Vermilion City<!-- (Japanese: '''''' '''')--> is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive facility in [[Kanto]], located in [[Vermilion City]]. [[Chloe]] and [[Goh]] attend the school and as such the location has appeared in several episodes of {{aniseries|JN}}.

Although mentioned for the first time in ''[[JN002|Legend? Go! Friends? Go!]]'', the place prominently appeared for the first time in ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]''.

==Staff==
===Goh and Chloe's teacher===
[[File:Vermilion school teacher.png|thumb|250px|Homeroom teacher]]
[[Goh]] and [[Chloe]]'s homeroom teacher is a recurring character in {{aniseries|JN}} who first appeared in ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]''. During a class, she asked her students about their aspirations in life. This question ended up leaving Chloe unsure about her future.

She appeared again in ''[[JN049|To Train, or Not to Train!]]'', this time meeting Goh and Chloe while they went to school. Goh revealed to Chloe that he made a deal with the teacher so that he can be at school during exams while traveling the [[Pokémon world]] for his work as a research assistant at the [[Cerise Laboratory]]. She was seen again during class applying the exam to her students until Chloe ended up having to leave in a hurry to see why {{TP|Professor Cerise|Yamper}} had entered the school.

In ''[[JN050|A Pinch of This, a Pinch of That!]]'', she sent an e-mail to Chloe, letting her know that she could write an assignment on her field trip to the [[Galar]] region to make up for her absence from class.

In ''[[JN087|Breaking the Ice!]]'', she was seen again welcoming [[Regina]] and later passing information about the school to her. The next day, she was with Goh, Chloe, Regina, and Ash when the group decided to create an ice park for the other students.

