===Goh's former teacher===
[[File:Teacher JN062.png|thumb|250px|Goh's former teacher]]
In a flashback of a few years before the events of ''[[JN062|Not Too Close for Comfort!]]'', a teacher approached Goh to question him about his loneliness and isolation from other students. Although she didn't realize it, these questions ended up making Goh feel too intimidated to answer.
{{-}}

==Known students==
===Goh and Chloe's class===
====Goh====
[[File:Goh School Uniform.png|thumb|250px|Goh]]
[[File:Goh Schoolwork.png|thumb|left|250px|Goh's schoolwork about Ash]]
{{main|Goh}}
With his work as a research assistant for the [[Cerise Laboratory]], Goh has only been attending school on exam days. As seen in ''[[JN002|Legend? Go! Friends? Go!]]'', Chloe sometimes gives him homework assigned to their class.

In ''[[JN049|To Train, or Not to Train!]]'', Goh went to school with Chloe to do one of the necessary exams. Later, he and Chloe ended up rescuing a lost {{TP|Chloe|Eevee}} and dealt with {{TRT}}, who tried to steal the Pokémon present at the school.

In ''[[JN062|Not Too Close for Comfort!]]'', a flashback from Goh showed what his life at school was like a few years before he met {{Ash}}.

In ''[[JN087|Breaking the Ice!]]'', Goh took {{Ash}} to the school to give a presentation on his friend and the way Ash views Pokémon.

{{-}}
====Chloe====
[[File:Chloe anime.png|thumb|250px|Chloe]]
{{main|Chloe}}
Unlike Goh, Chloe regularly attends classes and is often seen studying. In several episodes of {{aniseries|JN}}, Chloe can be seen going to or from school. 

In ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]'', Chloe was seen at school the first time. During a class on future aspirations, the teacher asks Chloe about her plans. She did not know how to answer the question, however.

In ''[[JN029|There's a New Kid in Town!]]'', Chloe was seen at school. She got lost in her thoughts about the [[Chloe#Pidove|Pidove]] her family rescued.

In ''[[JN038|Restore and Renew!]]'', Chloe had a school assignment to deliver, which, at [[Professor Cerise|her father]]'s suggestion, she ended up writing about [[Fossil|Fossil Pokémon]].

In ''[[JN049|To Train, or Not to Train!]]'', Chloe and Goh were seen going to school together. They planned on taking exams, but Chloe ended up finding an {{TP|Chloe|Eevee}} who had fled the [[Eevee Evolution Lab]].

In ''[[JN050|A Pinch of This, a Pinch of That!]]'', Chloe received an assignment about the [[Galar]] [[Fossil|Fossil Pokémon]] to make up for her absence from class while she traveled to the Galar [[region]] with {{Ash}} and Goh.

In ''[[JN062|Not Too Close for Comfort!]]'', in a flashback from Goh, a younger Chloe saw a teacher question Goh about his loneliness concerning the other students.

====Yeardley====
[[File:Yeardley.png|thumb|250px|Yeardley]]
{{main|Yeardley}}
'''Yeardley''' (Japanese: '''ユウト''' ''Yūto'') is a minor recurring character in {{aniseries|JN}}. Yeardley first appeared in ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]'', where he answered a question asked by his homeroom teacher.

In ''[[JN029|There's a New Kid in Town!]]'', he was present in Chloe's class. 

{{-}}
====Regina====
[[File:Regina.png|thumb|250px|Regina]]
{{main|Regina}}
'''Regina''' (Japanese: '''レジーナ''' ''Regina'') is a [[character of the day]] who appeared in ''[[JN087|Breaking the Ice!]]''. She is a recently transferred student who initially struggled to make new friends, but it changed when she grew closer to Chloe.

{{-}}
====Chloe's classmate====
[[File:Chloe classmate.png|thumb|130px|Chloe's classmate]]
This girl, who first appeared in ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]'', is a minor recurring character in {{aniseries|JN}}. She sits in front of [[Chloe]] in class. During class, when Chloe was asked about her future aspirations by their teacher, she asked Chloe if she wants to follow in her father's footsteps and become a [[Pokémon Professor]], which ended up making Chloe uncomfortable. Following this, she asked again if Chloe didn't like Pokémon.

In ''[[JN029|There's a New Kid in Town!]]'', she was seen again studying, while Chloe was thinking about the injured {{p|Pidove}} that her family rescued. She appeared again in ''[[JN049|To Train, or Not to Train!]]'', this time taking a test with the rest of the class.

She appeared briefly in ''[[JN087|Breaking the Ice!]]'', first welcoming [[Regina]] and then with students who were scared of Regina after an incident with her {{p|Glaceon}}. When Regina reconciled with the class, she joined the other students to play in the park made of ice by {{Ash}}, [[Goh]], and Regina's Pokémon.
{{-}}

==Places==
===Classrooms===
The classrooms at the school follow a structure very similar to that of a classroom in Japanese schools. It has a bigger slate in the center with a speaker (probably for school ads) and two smaller ones on the sides that have some ads. At the back of the room, there are a few more slates that work as a notice board and a small bookcase.
[[File:Vermilion City school classroom.png|thumb|center|250px|Classroom]]
{{-}}

===Pokémon Garden===
[[File:Vermilion City school playground.png|thumb|250px|Playground]]
The Pokémon Garden is used for students to leave their Pokémon while they are attending classes. In addition to toys designed for Pokémon, there are some made for humans as well. In ''[[JN049|To Train, or Not to Train!]]'', {{TRT}} disguised themselves as students to steal the Pokémon here.

